{"answers":[{"question_id":"region_a:q1","answer":"Region B law identified on the supplied facts does not impose an ordinary disclosure or access obligation on Harrow under the Health Records Act. Harrow is neither a covered provider nor a service agent, so Sections 4–8—including permitted-disclosure and security rules—do not apply to its described handling. Harrow also is not a data host on the facts because it keeps the referral in its own clinical record for its own care, rather than storing it on behalf of another person.

The principal Region B access risk is the Records Access Act. The Records Access Commissioner may order a "computing provider" to produce records stored by it or accessible to it for national security or the investigation of serious crime. Such an order needs no court authorisation and may be made regardless of the patient's nationality or residence. However, the facts do not establish that Harrow, or the referral-portal operator, is a computing provider: that status requires providing storage, hosting or computing services in Region B (or being incorporated in Region B and providing those services elsewhere). No order, investigation or national-security purpose is supplied. Accordingly, the possible production-order route remains fact-dependent rather than an identified present disclosure requirement.

On the stated material, no Region B rule has been shown that would prevent Harrow or a portal operator from complying with Commission-approved transfer clauses. If a qualifying computing provider received a valid Records Access Act production order, it would have a statutory production obligation; the supplied Region B provisions do not state that such an order is displaced by, or excuses compliance with, transfer clauses. Whether that would create a conflict with particular Commission-approved clauses depends on the clauses and any further facts about the operator, so the clause-compliance conclusion is limited to the Region B law read here.","facts":[{"fact_id":"f_3707d0e0f8a9","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_febc895bce9e","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_85110fb9a3e5","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_27f370d17c18","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_7e86304fe561","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_1d30f2f75c58","path":"","quote":""},{"fact_id":"f_a7a94423ed89","path":"","quote":""}],"citations":["B-HRA 2","B-HRA 3","B-RAA 2","B-RAA 3"],"quote_id":"B-RAA 3#L1","requirement_ids":["hra_sections_4_to_8_application","data_host_retention","records_access_production_order"]}],"requirements":[]}

